  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/41964498/v0.21.0</id>
    <updated>2022-05-30T15:06:39Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/prometheus/blackbox_exporter/releases/tag/v0.21.0"/>
    <title>0.21.0 / 2022-05-30</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;This Prometheus release is built with go1.18, which contains two noticeable&lt;br&gt;
changes related to TLS and HTTP:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://go.dev/doc/go1.18#tls10&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;TLS 1.0 and 1.1 disabled by default client-side&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
Blackbox Exporter users can override this with the &lt;code&gt;min_version&lt;/code&gt; parameter of&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/configuration/configuration/#tls_config&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;tls_config&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://go.dev/doc/go1.18#sha1&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Certificates signed with the SHA-1 hash function are rejected&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
This doesn&#39;t apply to self-signed root certificates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[BUGFIX] Prevent setting negative timeouts when using a small scrape interval. &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;1114014647&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/prometheus/blackbox_exporter/issues/869&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/prometheus/blackbox_exporter/pull/869/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/prometheus/blackbox_exporter/pull/869&quot;&gt;#869&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</content>
